english_source:
16165 — Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:
“There are seven whom Allah will shade in His shade on the Day when there will be no shade except His shade:
a just ruler;
a young person who grows up worshipping Allah;
a man whose heart remains attached to the mosque from the time he leaves it until he returns;
two men who love one another for the sake of Allah, meeting upon that love and parting upon it;
a man who remembers Allah while alone and his eyes overflow with tears;
a man who is invited by a woman of status and beauty but says, ‘Indeed, I fear Allah’;
and a man who gives charity and conceals it so completely that his left hand does not know what his right hand spends.”
Agreed upon: Narrated by Mālik in Kitāb al-Shiʿr (14), Muslim (1031), and al-Bukhārī (660).

